  {
   "id": 20,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    1560,
    1450
   ],
   "size": [
    430,
    900
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 19,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "# 09b Fixed location + pose + references\n\nThree things come from three separate places, each one contributing **only** what it is for:\n\n| What | Where it comes from | Why nothing else leaks in |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Background** | group 02, the location photo | `ImageCompositeMasked` pastes the generation back *inside the mask only*, so every pixel outside is bit-identical to your photo |\n| **Pose** | group 07, the pose photo | the photo is reduced to an OpenPose **stick-figure skeleton** first, so there is no face, clothing, lighting or background left to copy |\n| **Her** | group 01 character LoRA + group 06 reference photos | the LoRA holds the face, the references hold hair, make-up and clothes |\n\n## Use it\n1. **Group 02**: load the location photo. Right-click it -> **Open in MaskEditor** and paint where\n   she should appear (her whole body plus a little room). Save.\n2. **Group 07**: load any photo of anyone in the pose you want. Look at *Check the skeleton* after\n   the first run to confirm it was detected.\n3. **Group 06**: a clear photo of her in *Reference 1*. Ctrl+B on *Reference 2* to add an outfit\n   shot or a second angle.\n4. **Group 03**: describe the scene. Leave the pose out of `subject_action` -- the skeleton is in\n   charge of it. Keep `environment` matching the real photo so the lighting agrees. The\n   `extra` field holds the standing \"Picture 1 is her, Picture 3 is the skeleton\" instruction;\n   keep it. You never write the \"don't look AI\" wording: the Prompt Builder appends it to every\n   prompt by itself.\n5. **Queue.** Group 08 runs by itself: the background is blurred, then the camera pass adds ISO\n   grain, corner fringing, corner falloff and a white balance drift, and the result is saved to\n   `outputs/images/final/`. Nothing to set -- that is the whole point of it being here.\n\nSet once, then leave alone: groups 01, 04, 05, 08. Per picture you touch **02** (location +\nmask), **03** (prompt), and **06/07** when the reference or pose changes.\n\n## Knobs\n- **Picture numbers are fixed to the slots**, so Picture 3 is always the skeleton even when\n  Reference 2 is bypassed. Safe to refer to them in the prompt.\n- **Denoise is 1.0**: the masked area is built from scratch. Pose no longer needs to survive from\n  the latent, so nothing of the location photo's original contents bleeds into her.\n- **Grow mask** feathers the seam by 12px. Raise it if you see an outline, lower it if the\n  background gets eaten.\n- **Wrong scale?** Paint the mask the size you want her to be -- the model fills the shape.\n- **Skeleton too literal / not detected?** Ctrl+B the *Skeleton* node to drop the pose reference\n  entirely; the rest of the workflow keeps working.\n- **No references at all?** Also Ctrl+B the *Krea 2 image reference LoRA* in group 01 and the\n  Reference loaders, and it falls back to prompt-only inpainting.\n- **Grain too strong / too clean?** `iso_grain` on *Camera Imperfections*: 0.015 clean daylight,\n  0.025 ordinary phone photo, 0.05+ pushed high ISO. 0 turns it off.\n- **Same picture, different grain?** Set the *Sampler*'s control to `fixed` and queue again: only\n  the filters re-run (the generation is cached), so you get another grain roll in seconds."
   ],
   "color": "#222",
   "bgcolor": "#000"
  },
